\ matmul: the matrix.c loop called directly, against the size-dispatching matmul
\ that loading lib/statistics.telic installs over the same name — the loop below
\ 24x24 of work, cblas dgemm above it. Binding is early, so the built-in xt is
\ captured before the load and both stay callable afterwards. The second column
\ is therefore the dispatcher, and under the threshold it measures the same loop
\ plus the dispatch.
\ Square n x n operands, integer ramp data (so the products are exact and the
\ two can be compared for equality), result matrix freshly allocated by each
\ call, so both sides pay the same allocation and GC.
\
\ Run:  ./telic -b < bench/stats/matmul-native-vs-blas.telic

' matmul constant native-matmul

"statistics" load-library

( n -- m ) \ n x n ramp, deterministic
: ramp | n | 0 n n * 1- 1 matrix-range n n reshape ; internal

( n -- reps ) \ hold the work per size roughly constant, capped so the batches stay short
: reps-for | n | 20000000 n n * n * / round-down 20 max2 100000 min2 ; internal

( n -- flag ) \ do the two spellings answer the same matrix?
: agree? | n | n ramp to a  n ramp to b  a b native-matmul execute  a b matmul  = ; internal

( n reps -- ) \ time both spellings of the same product
: bench-size
	| n reps |
	n ramp to a
	n ramp to b

	\ one of each first, so neither pays a cold path in the timed loop
	a b native-matmul execute drop
	a b matmul drop

	\ the minimum over several batches: interference and GC only ever add time,
	\ so the fastest batch is the closest reading of the work itself
	1e18 to native-us
	0 5 1 do native-batch
		now to t0
		0 reps 1 do i  a b native-matmul execute drop  loop
		now t0 - reps / 1e6 * to trial
		trial native-us < if trial to native-us then
	loop

	1e18 to blas-us
	0 5 1 do blas-batch
		now to t0
		0 reps 1 do i  a b matmul drop  loop
		now t0 - reps / 1e6 * to trial
		trial blas-us < if trial to blas-us then
	loop

	n reps native-us blas-us  blas-us native-us /
	"{4}x{4}{tab}reps {3}{tab}native {2:.3f} us{tab}dispatched {1:.3f} us{tab}ratio {0:.2f}"
	format . cr ; internal

\ agreement first: a speed comparison of two different answers is worthless
[ 2 3 4 8 16 32 64 ] ' agree? map
[: 1 = :] all? "identical results at every checked size: {0}" format . cr
cr

[ 2 3 4 6 8 12 16 24 32 48 64 96 128 192 256 ]
[: dup reps-for bench-size :] each
